Here's a Dart function that returns the top three coins with the highest average profit and the top 3 coins with the highest average loss:

```dart
import 'package:collection/collection.dart';

List<String> getTopCoinsWithHighestAverageProfit(List<Transaction> transactions) {
  final groupedTransactions = transactions.groupBy((transaction) => transaction.coinName);
  final profitSummaries = groupedTransactions.map((key, value) {
    final totalProfit = value.fold<int>(0, (previousValue, currentValue) => previousValue + currentValue.profitEarned);
    final averageProfit = totalProfit / value.length;
    return MapEntry(key, averageProfit);
  });
  return profitSummaries.toList().take(3).map((entry) => entry.key).toList();
}

List<String> getTopCoinsWithHighestAverageLoss(List<Transaction> transactions) {
  final groupedTransactions = transactions.groupBy((transaction) => transaction.coinName);
  final lossSummaries = groupedTransactions.map((key, value) {
    final totalLoss = value.fold<int>(0, (previousValue, currentValue) => previousValue + currentValue.profitLost);
    final averageLoss = totalLoss / value.length;
    return MapEntry(key, averageLoss);
  });
  return lossSummaries.toList().take(3).map((entry) => entry.key).toList();
}
```

This function first groups the transactions by their coin name using the `groupBy()` method from the `collection` package. It then calculates the total profit or loss for each coin and divides it by the number of transactions to get the average profit or loss. Finally, it returns the top three coins with the highest average profit and the top three coins with the highest average loss.

