To create a NestJS model that creates a MongoDB document with multiple schemas, you can follow these steps:

1. Define your MongoDB schemas:

Create separate files for each schema, e.g., `user.schema.ts` and `product.schema.ts`. Each schema should define the structure of the corresponding document.

```typescript
// user.schema.ts
import { Schema, model } from 'mongoose';

const userSchema = new Schema({
  name: String,
  email: String,
});

export const User = model('User', userSchema);
```

2. Create your NestJS model:

In your `models` folder, create a file named `my-model.ts` and import the necessary dependencies.

```typescript
// models/my-model.ts
import { Model, model, Schema } from 'mongoose';
import { User } from './user.schema';
import { Product } from './product.schema';

const myModelSchema = new Schema({
  users: [User],
  products: [Product],
});

export const MyModel = model('MyModel', myModelSchema);
```

3. Use your NestJS model in your controller:

In your `controllers` folder, create a file named `my-controller.ts` and import the necessary dependencies.

```typescript
// controllers/my-controller.ts
import { Controller, Post } from '@nestjs/common';
import { MyModel } from '../models/my-model';

@Controller()
export class MyController {
  constructor(private readonly myModelService: MyModel) {}

  @Post()
