response:
You can modify the `checkMNPStatusAPI` function to update the state directly instead of creating a separate variable to store the response data. Here's an updated version of the function:

```javascript
checkMNPStatusAPI(phoneNo, index) {
  console.log("mnpphoneno: " + phoneNo);

  var headers = new Headers();
  headers.append("Authorization", "Bearer " + user.getAccessToken());
  fetch(api.checkPortInStatus(user.getProductCode(), phoneNo), {
    headers: headers,
    method: 'GET'
  })
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(rjson => {
      this.setState(prevState => ({
        registrations: prevState.registrations.map((reg, i) =>
          i === index ? { ...reg, mnpStatus: rjson.status } : reg
        )
      }));
    });
}
```

This code updates the state directly by using the `setState` function with a callback that takes the previous state as an argument. It then maps the `registrations` array and updates the `mnpStatus` property for the specific index (`index`) provided.

```powershell
# Get the domain SID
$domainSid = (Get-ADDomain).sid

# Function to check if a SID is present in the SIDHistory of any user or group in the domain
function CheckSIDInSIDHistory($sid) {
    $sidHistory = @()

    # Iterate through all users and groups in the domain
    Get-ADUser -Filter * -Properties SID, SIDHistory | ForEach-Object {
        $sidHistory += $_.SIDHistory
    }

    Get-ADGroup -Filter * -Properties SID, SIDHistory | ForEach-Object {
        $sidHistory += $_.SIDHistory
    }

    # Check if the SID is present in the SIDHistory
    return ($sidHistory | Where-Object { $_ -eq $sid }) -ne $null
}

# Recursively check folders for ACLs with SIDs in the SIDHistory
function CheckFolderACLs($folderPath) {
    $acl = Get-Acl -Path $folderPath
    $sidHistoryPresent = $false

    # Iterate through each access control entry (ACE) in the ACL
    foreach ($ace in $acl.Access) {
        if ($ace.IdentityReference -match "^S-1-5-21-") {
            $sid = New-Object System.Security.Principal.SecurityIdentifier($ace.IdentityReference)

            if (CheckSIDInSIDHistory($sid.Value)) {
                $sidHistoryPresent = $true
                break
            }
        }
    }

    if ($sidHistoryPresent) {
        Write-Host "Folder: $folderPath"
    }

    # Recursively check subfolders
    Get-ChildItem -Path $folderPath -Directory | ForEach-Object {
        CheckFolderACLs($_.FullName)
    }
}

# Start checking folder ACLs
CheckFolderACLs("C:\Path\To\Starting\Folder")
```

Replace `"C:\Path\To\Starting\Folder"` with the starting folder you want to check. This script will recursively check all folders within that starting folder
